module dcr_yield_stress_dimension_silent

// D3 decompose-phase RED before-image for PRD `docs/prds/v0_6/dimension-checked-readers.md`
// leaf β, boundary row B5 — AMENDED at decompose.
//
// PRD §8 B5 writes the fixture as a `Material` with `yield_stress: 310mm`, but
// `Material` (crates/reify-compiler/stdlib/materials_mechanical.ri:82) has NO
// `yield_stress` field — the PRD states this correctly in §2.4 correction 3 and
// then contradicts it in B5. MEASURED at decompose: writing it that way makes
// the argument silently lower to a POSITIONAL `__arg3: 0.31 m`, so the fixture
// would not exercise the intended reader at all.
//
// `yield_stress : Option<Pressure>` lives on `trait ElasticMaterial`
// (materials_fea.ri:114) and its conformers (`Steel_AISI_1045` at :157, default
// `some(310MPa)` at :161). This fixture uses the real field.
//
// MEASURED at decompose (2026-07-28, main efba5a8036): `reify eval` EXIT 0,
// ZERO diagnostics; `wrong` stores `yield_stress: Some(0.31 m)` where the
// default is `Some(310000000 kg*m^-1*s^-2)`. `material_field_si`
// (crates/reify-stdlib/src/flexures/common.rs:126) then reads 0.31 as Pa.
//
// NOTE for leaf α (contract §7): this is the `Option<Pressure>` shape.
// `accept_arg` (crates/reify-eval/src/arg_acceptance.rs:117-130) has NO
// `Value::Option` arm — it matches Undef / Scalar / `other => Rejected`. Making
// `validate_dimensioned_scalar` "a thin adapter over accept_arg" (§6 decision 8)
// WITHOUT adding Option-unwrapping would regress every `yield_stress` read to a
// rejection, because `scalar_si`/`material_field_si` deliberately recurse into
// `Option(Some(_))` (documented at common.rs:117-125).

structure def DcrYieldStressDimensionSilent {
    let wrong   = Steel_AISI_1045(yield_stress: some(310mm))
    let correct = Steel_AISI_1045()

    let j_wrong = prb_cantilever_beam(20mm, 5mm, 0.5mm, wrong, point3(0mm, 0mm, 0mm), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0))
    let j_ok    = prb_cantilever_beam(20mm, 5mm, 0.5mm, correct, point3(0mm, 0mm, 0mm), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0))
}
